{"seq":14,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-memory-skills-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:29:55.184Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"6951e9c5cc27308910f9f239a16fcbe48c7892d202ae60a67c89fc4df1318c4e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through every Moss note I can see on the shared drive (four North digests and two Central ones). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets turn up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift got through fine. Moss also had a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nSome things to check before this goes in the notes:\n• The two numbers look alike (4419 / 4492), and both involve Door 14 at the gatehouse. They're described as different problems (SMS vs. scanner), and the cheat sheet has no date. It's worth checking against the QFL ticket records that they really are two separate tickets.\n• The other two North digests (9/14/2025 pipeline and 3/23/2026 renewal) mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers.\n• I left out #4409, #4412 and FR-882 on purpose. They show up in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company (a competitor's customer, not ours), so it isn't included either."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-memory-skills-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:30:00.821Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b1ce6008853a544f24eb135bbd91f839ac400977be9c43b74b22fd437844f2f0","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I've replied to Dana in their DM. Moss's notes on the shared drive mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n- **#PD-4492:** from Moss's 5 Oct 2025 \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest. Drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18) weren't getting their door assignments by text. Support patched it on 4 Oct 2025, and Thea Ramaswell confirmed the next morning's shift got through fine.\n- **#4419:** from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\". The gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI also pointed out three things to Dana:\n- **Possible duplicate:** the two numbers look alike and both involve Door 14, so Dana should check the QFL ticket records to confirm they're really two separate tickets.\n- **Left out on purpose:** #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't our customer.\n- **Not searched:** I only looked at shared files any member can open, not channels or messages."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
